&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-item ui-form-item-horizontal&quot; data-direction=&quot;horizontal&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX is hiring Business Process Analysts to serve as the domain and functional authority for complex Army financial, transactional, and administrative processes. You will guide the extraction of legacy business logic from historical reporting tools and systems, transforming them into configurable modern workflows while ensuring strict adherence to statutory accounting validations, posting rules, and comprehensive audit logs. Your functional expertise will mitigate transition risks and prevent operational gaps during capability migrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze legacy custom-built database applications and document complex transactional workflows to translate them into platform-independent technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify potential process pitfalls, regulatory constraints, and operational impacts of migrating legacy capabilities out of mature enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map and translate legacy structures, master data configurations, and hierarchical accounting lines from various legacy transactional systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define validation rules for critical operational capabilities, including statement of transactions, account reclassifications, and funds distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate workshops with process owners, lead functional testing (UAT), and manage the transition of support responsibilities to long-term sustainment teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active U.S. Secret Clearance (or higher).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in business process implementation and solutioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience with SAP functional design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Army Business Processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in GFEBS solution design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;The SMX salary determination process takes into account a number of factors, including but not limited to, geographic location, Federal Government contract labor categories, relevant prior work experience, specific skills, education and certifications. At SMX, one of our Core Values is to Invest in Our People so we offer a competitive mix of compensation, learning &amp;amp; development opportunities, and benefits. Some key components of our robust benefits include health insurance, paid leave, and retirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The proposed salary for this position is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$112,600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$187,600 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SMX®, we are a team of technical and domain experts dedicated to enabling your mission. From priority national security initiatives for the DoD to highly assured and compliant solutions for healthcare, we understand that digital transformation is key to your future success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We share your vision for the future and strive to accelerate your impact on the world. We bring both cutting edge technology and an expansive view of what’s possible to every engagement. Our delivery model and unique approaches harness our deep technical and domain knowledge, providing forward-looking insights and practical solutions to power secure mission acceleration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX is an Equal Opportunity employer including disabilities and veterans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;message-body-1758638857922&quot; class=&quot;fui-ChatMyMessage__body rcngbzt ___eyw0iv0 f10pi13n ftqa4ok f2hkw1w f8hki3x f1d2448m f1bjia2o ffh67wi f1j6vpng f1pniga2 f987i1v f1ffjurs f15bsgw9 f14e48fq f18yb2kv fd6o370 ffwy5si f3znvyf f57olzd f4stah7 f480a47 fs1por5 fk6fouc figsok6 fkhj508 f19n0e5 f9ijwd5 fzqqayd f10ostut f1o0qvyv f9ggezi f1xp5gbu f150uoa4 ffyari3 fo7qwa0 f16xkysk fxowb0n f11ghf3q f13aoclr flypziy f10kwr27 fquw1qa fftr39l f13lathq f15hsm81 f2ss68y ffb60jq f8nuap2 f13nk4fk f7jacry fq08z5q fd9af6s fr74w9q fcl9uv6 f13sm7pj f1u6qqly f16wpxbl faim3u9 f6cs3qo fa2w2z3 fd39nx6 f10gn8j9 frcqmxy f1w9ws4k f1ddxkqj fd10euv fvuz61 f1nbc6gw&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;content-1758638857922&quot; class=&quot;fui-Primitive ___16zla5h f1oy3dpc fqtknz5 fyvcxda&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;x_Signature&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Selected applicant may be subject to a background investigation and/or education verification.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX does not sponsor a new applicant for employment authorization or immigration related support for this position (i.e. H1B, F-1 OPT, F-1 STEM OPT, F-1 CPT, J-1, TN, E-2, E-3, L-1 and O-1, or any EADs or other forms of work authorization that require immigration support from an employer).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-item ui-form-item-horizontal&quot; data-direction=&quot;horizontal&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring an Army ERP Functional consultant to aid our clients by analyzing their Financial and Logistics datasets to support Enterprise financial analytics. The successful candidate will be expected to work closely with our clients to support modernization and determine the functional logic to integrate datasets from Army ERP’s and Legacy Accounting, Budgeting and Costing systems. The consultant will help our clients navigate a complex and dynamic business landscape. This role requires strong Techno/Functional expertise of the Army’s financial business processes and business mission area financial systems, enabling effective creation and integration analytical solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze financial and logistics datasets from Army and DoW systems to determine the integration logic to enable Enterprise reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Normalize data from SAP and Non-SAP systems to consolidate in datamarts to support HQDA and Command level reports and dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the Financials subject matter expert across highly diverse mission fields and throughout U.S. government stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with multi-disciplinary teams in a rapidly changing mission-oriented work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess and apply knowledge of the Department of the Army financial systems and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the management and tracking of project timelines and deliverables keeping the client and stakeholders informed of progress and any challenges encountered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently lead functional workshops and meetings to clarify data integration logic and related dependencies as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Secret security clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of Ten (10) years of experience in Army ERP implementation and support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in General Fund Enterprise Business System (GFEBS) data to include Budgeting and Expenditure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of Army’s Financial Line of Accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert level knowledge of how Army’s Financial data traverses’ different ERP and Legacy systems based on the different business processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert level knowledge of SAP and the functional impacts of config. changes to FI, FM, CO, MM, PP modules, on transactional postings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert level knowledge of US Treasury Financial reporting, related data elements and how the Treasury systems interact with the Army Financial systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing Enterprise Data Warehouse and Data Lake to support HDQA and command level reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Army financial management and business process re-engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the Army’s General Fund Enterprise Business System (GFEBS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in information technology, Computer Science, Business Administration, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and analytical abilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Desired Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Global Combat Support System-Army (GCSS-Army)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writing queries and programming in SQL or PySpark&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working in Palantir Foundry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;The SMX salary determination process takes into account a number of factors, including but not limited to, geographic location, Federal Government contract labor categories, relevant prior work experience, specific skills, education and certifications. At SMX, one of our Core Values is to Invest in Our People so we offer a competitive mix of compensation, learning &amp;amp; development opportunities, and benefits. Some key components of our robust benefits include health insurance, paid leave, and retirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The proposed salary for this position is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$140,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$230,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SMX®, we are a team of technical and domain experts dedicated to enabling your mission. From priority national security initiatives for the DoD to highly assured and compliant solutions for healthcare, we understand that digital transformation is key to your future success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We share your vision for the future and strive to accelerate your impact on the world. We bring both cutting edge technology and an expansive view of what’s possible to every engagement. Our delivery model and unique approaches harness our deep technical and domain knowledge, providing forward-looking insights and practical solutions to power secure mission acceleration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX is an Equal Opportunity employer including disabilities and veterans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;message-body-1758638857922&quot; class=&quot;fui-ChatMyMessage__body rcngbzt ___eyw0iv0 f10pi13n ftqa4ok f2hkw1w f8hki3x f1d2448m f1bjia2o ffh67wi f1j6vpng f1pniga2 f987i1v f1ffjurs f15bsgw9 f14e48fq f18yb2kv fd6o370 ffwy5si f3znvyf f57olzd f4stah7 f480a47 fs1por5 fk6fouc figsok6 fkhj508 f19n0e5 f9ijwd5 fzqqayd f10ostut f1o0qvyv f9ggezi f1xp5gbu f150uoa4 ffyari3 fo7qwa0 f16xkysk fxowb0n f11ghf3q f13aoclr flypziy f10kwr27 fquw1qa fftr39l f13lathq f15hsm81 f2ss68y ffb60jq f8nuap2 f13nk4fk f7jacry fq08z5q fd9af6s fr74w9q fcl9uv6 f13sm7pj f1u6qqly f16wpxbl faim3u9 f6cs3qo fa2w2z3 fd39nx6 f10gn8j9 frcqmxy f1w9ws4k f1ddxkqj fd10euv fvuz61 f1nbc6gw&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;content-1758638857922&quot; class=&quot;fui-Primitive ___16zla5h f1oy3dpc fqtknz5 fyvcxda&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;x_Signature&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Selected applicant may be subject to a background investigation and/or education verification.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX does not sponsor a new applicant for employment authorization or immigration related support for this position (i.e. H1B, F-1 OPT, F-1 STEM OPT, F-1 CPT, J-1, TN, E-2, E-3, L-1 and O-1, or any EADs or other forms of work authorization that require immigration support from an employer).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-item ui-form-item-horizontal&quot; data-direction=&quot;horizontal&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX is seeking an Audio Visual (A/V) Support Specialist to provide information technology system engineering, cable plant technology support, system administration, and technical services for tactical systems and networks across a variety of platforms. This is an on-site role supporting multiple clients in Stuttgart, Germany, with less than 10% travel expected&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an A/V Support Specialist, you will oversee the design, installation, operation, and maintenance of A/V control systems (including Crestron and AMX), Video Teleconferencing (VTC) systems, Internet Protocol Television (IPTV) networks, and related infrastructure. Responsibilities include ongoing sustainment, troubleshooting, and repair of network cabling (CAT6 and fiber optic) as well as support for executive and command-level technical systems. You will join a team providing executive support for multiple command staff departments and work both to maintain and enhance the organization’s technical capabilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position requires a Department of Defense Top Secret clearance with SCI eligibility and U.S. citizenship&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and maintain conference rooms, executive suites, and desktop conferencing solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, install, operate, and maintain A/V systems and networked communication equipment, including VTC (Cisco and Microsoft Teams), display devices, microphones, and speakers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program, service, and troubleshoot integrated A/V and telecommunication platforms such as Crestron, AMX, Vaddio, Tesira, Extron, and Cisco&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Command, Control, Communications, Computers, Intelligence, Surveillance, and Reconnaissance (C5ISR) systems, including networking, voice, and satellite communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform installation, testing, splicing, terminations, and repair for CAT6 and fiber optic cabling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate and collaborate effectively with senior military personnel, customers, and technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Cybersecurity, Data Science, Information Systems, or Computer Science from an ABET-accredited or CAE-designated institution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current Cloud+, GICSP, SSCP, Security+, or GSEC certification (higher-level certifications such as CASP+, CCNA, CCNP Security, or CCSP are also accepted)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of three years’ experience in computer networking and A/V communications installation and support with platforms such as Crestron, AMX, Tesira, Extron, and IPTV&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Top Secret clearance with SCI eligibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with installation and maintenance of Cisco VTC and fiber optic/structured cabling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical problem-solving abilities, teamwork skills, and a systematic approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with network infrastructure and security, including Netgear and Cisco managed switches, DNS, DHCP, and multicast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced certifications such as CompTIA Advanced Security Practitioner (CASP+)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with server environments, including Windows Server, SharePoint, Exchange, Linux, VMware, and Cisco Unified Communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Call Manager software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current or eligible ECOPS/TESA Technical Expert Status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive, detail-oriented, and self-motivated team player&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;#CJPOST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;The SMX salary determination process takes into account a number of factors, including but not limited to, geographic location, Federal Government contract labor categories, relevant prior work experience, specific skills, education and certifications. At SMX, one of our Core Values is to Invest in Our People so we offer a competitive mix of compensation, learning &amp;amp; development opportunities, and benefits. Some key components of our robust benefits include health insurance, paid leave, and retirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The proposed salary for this position is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$110,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$125,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SMX®, we are a team of technical and domain experts dedicated to enabling your mission. From priority national security initiatives for the DoD to highly assured and compliant solutions for healthcare, we understand that digital transformation is key to your future success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We share your vision for the future and strive to accelerate your impact on the world. We bring both cutting edge technology and an expansive view of what’s possible to every engagement. Our delivery model and unique approaches harness our deep technical and domain knowledge, providing forward-looking insights and practical solutions to power secure mission acceleration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX is an Equal Opportunity employer including disabilities and veterans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;message-body-1758638857922&quot; class=&quot;fui-ChatMyMessage__body rcngbzt ___eyw0iv0 f10pi13n ftqa4ok f2hkw1w f8hki3x f1d2448m f1bjia2o ffh67wi f1j6vpng f1pniga2 f987i1v f1ffjurs f15bsgw9 f14e48fq f18yb2kv fd6o370 ffwy5si f3znvyf f57olzd f4stah7 f480a47 fs1por5 fk6fouc figsok6 fkhj508 f19n0e5 f9ijwd5 fzqqayd f10ostut f1o0qvyv f9ggezi f1xp5gbu f150uoa4 ffyari3 fo7qwa0 f16xkysk fxowb0n f11ghf3q f13aoclr flypziy f10kwr27 fquw1qa fftr39l f13lathq f15hsm81 f2ss68y ffb60jq f8nuap2 f13nk4fk f7jacry fq08z5q fd9af6s fr74w9q fcl9uv6 f13sm7pj f1u6qqly f16wpxbl faim3u9 f6cs3qo fa2w2z3 fd39nx6 f10gn8j9 frcqmxy f1w9ws4k f1ddxkqj fd10euv fvuz61 f1nbc6gw&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;content-1758638857922&quot; class=&quot;fui-Primitive ___16zla5h f1oy3dpc fqtknz5 fyvcxda&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;x_Signature&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Selected applicant may be subject to a background investigation and/or education verification.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX does not sponsor a new applicant for employment authorization or immigration related support for this position (i.e. H1B, F-1 OPT, F-1 STEM OPT, F-1 CPT, J-1, TN, E-2, E-3, L-1 and O-1, or any EADs or other forms of work authorization that require immigration support from an employer).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-item ui-form-item-horizontal&quot; data-direction=&quot;horizontal&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;m-b break-word ng-scope&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ng-scope&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;pre-wrap ng-binding ng-scope&quot;&gt;SMX is seeking an AWS Full Stack Applications Architect to design, build, and govern secure, highly available, and resilient full-stack applications natively integrated into the AWS ecosystem. This role blends hands-on coding and prototyping with high-level system design, technical governance, and mentorship of cross-functional teams. You will be responsible for creating scalable reference architectures and ensuring the technical excellence of cloud-native solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formulate scalable reference architectures using AWS core services (e.g., Lambda, ECS, API Gateway, S3, RDS, DynamoDB) conforming to the AWS Well-Architected Framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee or co-create modern front-end interfaces (React, Angular) and robust back-end APIs/microservices (Python, Node.js).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design performant relational (SQL) and non-relational (NoSQL) data storage layers alongside event-driven data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for and implement automated deployment pipelines using Infrastructure as Code (Terraform, AWS CloudFormation) and containerization (Docker, Kubernetes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead code reviews, troubleshoot complex system bottlenecks, and mentor full-stack engineering cohorts on development best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a project team developing AI apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8-10 years of professional experience in software engineering, with at least 3-5 years focused on cloud architecture and distributed application design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Secret security clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CompTIA Security+ certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with front-end technologies such as React or Angular.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with back-end languages such as Python or Node.js.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with core AWS services including Lambda, ECS/EKS, API Gateway, S3, RDS, and DynamoDB.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Infrastructure as Code (CloudFormation/Terraform) and CI/CD tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to interface with customers and optimize internal and external communications, with excellent written, verbal, and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven organizational skills with the ability to set priorities, multi-task, and analyze project scopes to recommend improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A detail-oriented self-starter and problem-solver, capable of working with minimal supervision to produce high-quality deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Desired Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS Certified Solutions Architect (Associate or Professional) or AWS Certified Developer.&lt;/li&gt;
