&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX is seeking a dynamic Sr. Program Manager to lead a large-scale, mission-critical IT modernization and transformation program for a federal agency focused on national security and law enforcement. The Program Manager will lead a large, multi-disciplinary team of experts in driving this transformation, ensuring the quality and timely delivery of a large-scale portfolio of projects. This role requires a strategic leader with deep technical expertise, exceptional problem-solving skills, and a proven ability to manage complex programs supporting critical government missions.&amp;nbsp;This position is onsite in Camp Springs, Maryland and requires a Top-Secret clearance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Essential Duties&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee major segments of complex technology projects, including defining technical objectives, project goals, data requirements, and appropriate methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a large program (100+ FTEs) across multiple service domains, including enterprise integration, case management, DevSecOps, large data processing, and advanced analytics services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct the development, implementation, and integration of an enterprise architecture for the capture, storage, and sharing of sensitive data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage program schedules, budgets (exceeding $100M), staffing levels, and resource allocation to ensure successful delivery of all project outputs and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic coaching and mentoring to senior executive staff on program governance, agile transformation, and organizational culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary interface with senior government stakeholders, developing and maintaining strong customer relationships to ensure alignment and program success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply deep technical expertise to adapt to evolving requirements and guide teams in delivering innovative, cost-effective solutions using Agile and Lean methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Technical &amp;amp; Methodological Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;chat-assistant w-full min-w-full markdown-prose svelte-1qscqw6&quot;&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;response-content-container&quot; class=&quot;w-full flex flex-col relative &quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing programs delivering DevSecOps, enterprise case management, and large-scale data analytics solutions in a cloud-native environment (e.g., AWS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with programs leveraging modern data science techniques and technologies, including Natural Language Processing (NLP), Large Language Models (LLM), and Named Entity Recognition (NER), for processing sensitive data.&lt;/li&gt;
