&lt;p&gt;SMX is looking for a highly motivated &lt;strong&gt;Junior Systems Administrator&lt;/strong&gt; with demonstrated experience to maintain the various systems used in a Software Development program. This position will provide support at Patuxent River NAS in southern Maryland.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Junior Systems Administrator, you will join a team of highly-driven, supportive, and skilled professionals engaged in supporting program management, technical, or business case analysis across the NAVAIR community.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Junior Systems Administrator will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install, configure, and support an organization&#39;s local area network (LAN), wide area network (WAN), and Internet systems or a segment of a network system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor network to ensure network availability to all system users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in network modeling, analysis, planning, and coordination&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze, test, troubleshoot, and evaluate existing network systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform maintenance to ensure networks operate correctly with minimal interruption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the efforts of less senior staff and/or be responsible for the efforts of all staff assigned to a specific job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize the functionality and performance of hardware and software systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain backup and disaster recovery plans and capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan for authorized service interruptions and outages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to unexpected or unauthorized service interruptions and outages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose software and hardware failures to resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and ensure security preventive measures are fully functioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test operating system and software upgrades, patches, and hot fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearance Required: Top Secret&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS or BA degree in a Technical Discipline
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma and 6 years’ additional experience within these functional duties; or an associate&#39;s degree and 4 additional years may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least one year of experience in system administration, performing the functional duties for this position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operating System certificate (Linux) and COMPTIA Security + or other DOD INST 8570 compliant qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of system administration principles, theories, and concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Linux OS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
