&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Linux/macOS Systems Administrator to support enterprise IT infrastructure onsite at NAS Patuxent River, MD. This position is responsible for administering, maintaining, and securing Linux and macOS systems across classified and unclassified environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have experience with Linux system administration, macOS endpoint management, and cybersecurity compliance. This role will leverage VMware Workspace ONE Unified Endpoint Management (UEM) to manage and secure endpoints while supporting daily operations, troubleshooting, and system maintenance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a self-starter who is comfortable working independently, learning new technologies, and collaborating with technical teams to support mission requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install, configure, administer, maintain, and troubleshoot Linux and macOS operating systems across enterprise IT environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and secure Linux and macOS endpoints using VMware Workspace ONE Unified Endpoint Management (UEM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, deploy, and maintain endpoint configurations, security policies, compliance profiles, and software packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain DISA Security Technical Implementation Guides (STIGs) to support compliance with DoD cybersecurity requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform vulnerability assessments, analyze findings, and coordinate remediation activities using ACAS and other approved security tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor system performance, availability, and security to identify and resolve operational issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform operating system updates, security patching, software installations, and routine system maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot hardware, software, operating system, and network connectivity issues affecting Linux and macOS environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the administration and maintenance of systems operating within classified and unclassified environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cybersecurity, engineering, and infrastructure teams to resolve technical issues and implement system improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate system documentation, configuration records, standard operating procedures, and troubleshooting guides.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve system reliability, security, automation, and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical support to customers and stakeholders, ensuring timely resolution of incidents and service requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform additional duties as assigned to support operational and mission requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
