&lt;p&gt;SMX is looking for a highly motivated&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Network Administrator&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;to join our growing team in Patuxent River, MD!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position will provide onsite support at Patuxent River NAS in southern Maryland and requires a &lt;strong&gt;DoD Top Secret&lt;/strong&gt; Security clearance which requires US citizenship for work on DoD contracts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Network Administrator, you will join a team of highly-driven, supportive, and skilled professionals engaged in supporting program management, technical, or business case analysis across the NAVAIR community.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties and Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and administer all network devices including deployment of new technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot LAN, WAN, and application-level connectivity and performance problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain network boundary security&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in network security incident investigations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform audit reviews of STIG standards and STIG updates of assigned devices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform reviews of vulnerabilities and perform remediation planning and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain documentation including work instructions, SOPs, processes and desk guides&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other tasks as assigned by customer POCs, Team Lead, and Management team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearance Required: Top Secret
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secret required to start&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IAT Level 2 or higher certification (Examples of minimum acceptable certifications-CCNA Security, CySA+, G SEC, Security+ CE, SSCP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-year minimum experience with networking device configuration and support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-year minimum experience with IP networking design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-year minimum experience with virtual server environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of DoD Information Assurance practices, including Security Technical Implementation Guide (STIG)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to interact with peers, management, and senior engineers in a constantly evolving environment to ensure a positive customer experience and atmosphere in the workplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to follow defined and documented customer processes and policies, and perform tasking where there may be documentation gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with network infrastructure devices and protocols, and proven ability to design, deploy, and maintain solutions supporting high-availability network infrastructures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be highly motivated and will be required to respond to and provide resolutions to problems on a timely basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with planning, configuring, managing, monitoring and troubleshooting of a variety of network systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Linux is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be a self-starter and have the initiative to learn more advanced operations and technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
