&lt;p&gt;SMX is seeking a Network Administrator to join our team supporting NAVAIR at Patuxent River, MD. This is a mid-level role supporting enterprise network infrastructure, boundary services, cybersecurity compliance, and modernization efforts across a large DoD environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position requires approximately 2–3 days onsite each week at Patuxent River, MD.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is a great opportunity for a network professional looking to expand their experience with Cisco, F5, enterprise networking, cybersecurity, and cloud modernization while working alongside experienced engineering and operations teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot LAN, WAN, and application-level connectivity and performance issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure, maintain, and troubleshoot Cisco switches, routers, and other network infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and administer F5 BIG-IP devices and load balancing services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy new network devices in accordance with approved engineering designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support highly available network architectures and traffic management solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain boundary security infrastructure supporting NAVAIR core sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with NCDOC, NAVAIR Information Assurance, and Program Management teams to investigate network security incidents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support DoD Public Key Infrastructure (PKI) enablement efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support NMCI/legacy network interoperability and cloud migration initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review STIG requirements and updates and support remediation of identified vulnerabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with network documentation, SOPs, work instructions, processes, and desk guides&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Windows, Unix/Linux, cybersecurity, cloud, engineering, and other infrastructure teams supporting the Data Center&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in an on-call rotation and scheduled off-hours maintenance windows as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearance Required: Top Secret
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A secret clearance may be considered to start, but candidates must be eligible for upgrade to Top Secret&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US Citizenship is required for work on DOW contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;DoD 8570/8140 IAT Level II compliant certification, such as Security+, CySA+, GSEC, SSCP, or another qualifying certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience supporting network infrastructure, Cisco devices, IP networking, or related enterprise network environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience configuring, monitoring, maintaining, or troubleshooting network systems and infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with enterprise networking concepts, protocols, and highly available network environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of DoD cybersecurity practices, including Security Technical Implementation Guides (STIGs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting, communication, and documentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with technical teams and customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Desired Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience configuring and supporting Cisco Catalyst and Nexus switches, including VLANs, trunking, routing, and network troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering Cisco Firepower firewalls or comparable enterprise firewall/security platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience configuring and supporting F5 BIG-IP, including load balancing, virtual servers, pools, health monitors, and traffic management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting network boundary infrastructure, including firewalls, routing, access controls, and secure connectivity between network environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with common enterprise networking protocols and services, including TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, BGP, OSPF, SNMP, and 802.1Q&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing Cisco IOS/NX-OS configuration, maintenance, upgrades, and troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying DISA STIGs, reviewing vulnerability findings, and remediating network-device security findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting network infrastructure within a DoD, NAVAIR, or other regulated enterprise environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience troubleshooting connectivity across physical, virtual, and cloud-hosted environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and maintaining network diagrams, device configurations, SOPs, and technical documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
