&lt;p&gt;SMX is seeking an experienced Tactical Mission Network (TMN) Trainers to deliver the Operator Lethality Course to tactical-level users on-site in Taiwan. This role is responsible for delivering training plans for end-users of the capabilities of the network.&amp;nbsp; The Training Specialist will support training events at various locations domestically and overseas, including potentially austere or conflict-adjacent environments, as determined by the client.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position requires a DoD Secret security clearance which requires US citizenship for work on DoD contracts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instruction &amp;amp; Course Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver the Operator Lethality Course curriculum to tactical-level military personnel, covering the full suite of TMN tools, their functionality, and practical field applications across all assigned training events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead hands-on practical exercises and scenario-based vignettes designed to reinforce operator proficiency with tactical mission network capabilities, joint fires integration, and remote advise and assist tactics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incorporate current real-world lessons learned from ongoing conflicts, including commercial data integration for operational preparation of the environment (OPE), unmanned systems employment, and C2 integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate, set up, and troubleshoot all training systems, end-user devices (EUDs), and unmanned systems (drones) prior to and during each training event&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adhere to the standardized lesson plan and course schedule provided by the Training Lead, delivering up to 8 hours of instruction per day across 4–5 day training events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compressed course schedules when pre-coordinated with the Training Lead and client&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Student Assessment &amp;amp; Feedback&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead after-action reviews (AARs) and student feedback sessions at the conclusion of each training event&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess student comprehension and performance throughout the course, providing real-time coaching and remediation as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Submit all student rosters, attendance records, and feedback results to the Training Lead following each event&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics &amp;amp; Event Coordination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with the on-ground unit point of contact to confirm facility, device, roster, and logistical requirements prior to training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pack, transport, and maintain accountability of all training equipment, including EUDs, drones, and Pelican-cased equipment kits, ensuring proper handling during transit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct pre-deployment site surveys when traveling the night prior to training kick-off, confirming setup and coordination with the on-ground POC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and test all network infrastructure, end-user devices, and demonstration systems prior to course commencements and drone systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All travel governed by Federal Joint Travel Regulations (JTR) and applicable contract requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience operating tactical mission network platforms, C2 systems, or related capabilities in a military or special operations context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active secret security clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated hands-on experience with end-user devices (EUDs) and unmanned systems (drones) in a tactical or operational environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FAA Part 107 Remote Pilot Certificate or equivalent military UAS operator qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience as a military instructor, trainer, or subject matter expert (SME) delivering formal or operational training to military audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel CONUS and OCONUS on short notice, including to austere and potentially high-risk locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and facilitation skills; ability to explain complex technical capabilities in operationally relevant terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in special operations, joint fires, targeting, or C4ISR systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with commercial data integration tools for operational preparation of the environment (OPE)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with advise and assist mission sets and partner force training environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with remote advise and assist tactics utilizing tactical mission networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing or revising programs of instruction (POI) or training materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior deployment experience to OCONUS locations in support of combat or contingency operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
