&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-item ui-form-item-horizontal&quot; data-direction=&quot;horizontal&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX is seeking a Project &amp;amp; Revenue Accounting SME. The Project &amp;amp; Revenue Accounting SME reports directly to the Senior Director, Finance and serves as a subject matter expert for project and revenue accounting. This role is responsible for ensuring accurate and timely revenue recognition, supporting an effective month- and quarter-end close, maintaining compliance with GAAP and ASC 606, and driving improvements that strengthen financial reporting, controls, and operational efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate brings deep experience in project accounting and revenue recognition within a highly regulated environment, expert knowledge of ASC 606, advanced Excel and Costpoint capabilities, and the ability to independently analyze complex issues and partner effectively across Finance, Accounting, Contracts, and Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a subject matter expert for project and revenue accounting, providing technical guidance and issue resolution across all levels of the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure revenue is recognized accurately and timely in accordance with ASC 606, ASC 340, GAAP, applicable contract terms, and Company policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide advanced technical support and troubleshooting for Costpoint, including revenue formulas, project configuration, and revenue-related system issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Business Unit Finance Leads, Program Managers, Contracts, and Accounting to ensure project setup, contract structures, and system configurations support appropriate revenue recognition and financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead key aspects of the month- and quarter-end close, including unbilled revenue reviews, revenue-at-risk analysis, project cost and profitability fluctuations, revenue adjustments, and identification and resolution of accounting issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and resolve complex unbilled and revenue-related issues, maintaining strong audit readiness and ensuring appropriate documentation and support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver detailed financial analyses and reporting to identify trends, anomalies, revenue recognition risks, project-level issues, and opportunities for corrective action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret complex contracts and apply revenue recognition methodologies across CPFF, CPAF, T&amp;amp;M, FFP, Commercial, and other contract types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor revenue accounting controls; identify control gaps and opportunities to strengthen the revenue accounting environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support DCAA, DCMA, interim, and annual financial statement audits, including requests related to revenue look-backs, unbilled balances, revenue timing, and ASC 606 compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with a high degree of independence, sound judgment, and accountability while serving as a trusted advisor to Finance and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills/Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of current, consecutive experience in project accounting and revenue recognition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert knowledge of ASC 606 and strong working knowledge of GAAP, FAR, and accounting requirements applicable to highly regulated environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience supporting DCAA and DCMA audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current, hands-on experience with Deltek Costpoint, preferably Costpoint 8.2.2026.3 or the current production version.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recent experience with Cognos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced/Expert Excel skills, including the ability to analyze large data sets and develop sophisticated financial analyses and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to troubleshoot complex Costpoint and revenue accounting issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current experience applying revenue recognition methodologies across multiple contract types, including CPFF, CPAF, T&amp;amp;M, FFP, and Commercial contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and exceptional attention to detail, with the ability to identify issues, assess risk, determine root causes, and drive resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work effectively in a fast-paced accounting organization; experience in a private equity-backed environment is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to bridge Finance, Accounting, Contracts, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independent, critical thinker who can quickly become effective in the role and requires limited supervision and onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills/Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current, hands-on experience with Deltek Costpoint, preferably Costpoint 8.2.2026.3 or the current production version.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recent experience with Cognos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work effectively in a fast-paced accounting organization; experience in a private equity-backed environment is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
