&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX is seeking a Senior Systems Engineer – Live Virtual Constructive (LVC) Training Systems to support the Tactical Combat Training System Increment II (TCTS II) / ATLaS program within the Naval Aviation Training Systems and Ranges Program Office (PMA-205) at Patuxent River Naval Air Station in Lexington Park, MD.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PMA-205 provides full lifecycle acquisition of naval aviation platforms and general training systems, training range instrumentation systems, and distributed mission training centers. The TCTS II is a next generation secure, Live-Virtual-Constructive (LVC) enabling, air combat training system that offers realistic threat scenarios and secure cross-service training.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is hybrid with local telework and on-site at NAS Patuxent River as required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs programmatic or technical leadership roles in an organization, identifying, formulating, designing, and/or testing practical solutions to engineering problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employs systems engineering methods and tools in the development of advanced complex systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assists with the LVC architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Address emerging technical and architecture questions regarding the Live (aircraft)-Virtual (simulations)-Constructive (synthetic threat) LVC elements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sets up processes for configuration control of interfaces between the TCTSII ground system and weapons models/constructive entity generating software systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sets up processes for configuration control of the interfaces between the TCTSII system and the aircraft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan for and implement the PMA-205 portions of the LVC Capabilities Requirements Document (CRD)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guides the engineering development of modern complex systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearance Required: Top Secret
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TS/SCI eligibility is a plus - this program will require access to SAP and potentially SCI programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US Citizenship is required for work on DoW contract&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical or Scientific MS or MA degree from an accredited college or university
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical or Scientific BS or BA degree from an accredited college or university and an additional four (4) years of recent and relevant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least ten (10) years of recent and relevant experience in an engineering position, three (3) of which must be directly related to DoD systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in an area of engineering expertise is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communications and teamwork skills working in a collaborative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;#cjpost #LI-HYBRID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
