&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;SMX is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Senior SharePoint Developer&lt;/strong&gt; to architect, deploy, and maintain custom SharePoint environments supporting Knowledge Management, the Analyst Production Toolkit, Control Access Programs, and PRESS Business Analytics. The developer will also migrate legacy workflows to Power Automate/Power Apps, implement secure access controls and DIA‑compliant governance, and produce UI/UX standards, documentation, and SOPs for site owners and end users.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a full-time onsite position in Ft. Meade, MD.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain SharePoint sites associated with Knowledge Management, Analyst Production Toolkit, Control Access Program, and PRESS Business Analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, deploy, and maintain custom SharePoint environments supporting Knowledge Management, the Analyst Production Toolkit, Control Access Programs (CAP), and PRESS Business Analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Migrate legacy workflows to automated Power Automate / Power Apps solutions to optimize intelligence analyst production lifecycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure SharePoint lists, libraries, and taxonomy schemas to feed operational data into PRESS Business Analytics dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement granular access controls, security group governance, and Active Directory integration to protect sensitive Control Access Program repositories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply DoD and DIA data governance, information management, and compliance standards across all managed sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce UI/UX design standards, technical documentation, and Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) for site owners and end-users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills, Experience &amp;amp; Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Duty Locations: ACIC (Fort George G. Meade, MD)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security Clearance: TS/SCI (Polygraph eligible / must submit if requested)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: Bachelor’s degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Knowledge Management, or a related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience Required: 4 to 6 years of specialized experience in SharePoint ecosystems (SharePoint Online, Microsoft 365, Power Platform), with at least 2 years focused on enterprise content management and structural taxonomy design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in the SharePoint Framework (SPFx) for building custom client-side web parts and application customizers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced command of the Microsoft Power Platform (Power Automate, Power Apps) for complex workflow automation and custom application forms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in web technologies (HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript/TypeScript) and SharePoint REST APIs / Microsoft Graph API&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth understanding of enterprise SharePoint architecture: Hub Sites, Site Collections, Content Types, Managed Metadata, and Term Store services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience querying project management and IT service management APIs (Jira, Git, ServiceNow) to extract operational metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
