&lt;div id=&quot;x_Signature&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Selected applicant may be subject to a background investigation and/or education verification.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX does not sponsor a new applicant for employment authorization or immigration related support for this position (i.e. H1B, F-1 OPT, F-1 STEM OPT, F-1 CPT, J-1, TN, E-2, E-3, L-1 and O-1, or any EADs or other forms of work authorization that require immigration support from an employer).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-item ui-form-item-horizontal&quot; data-direction=&quot;horizontal&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ui-form-field lifesuite__rte--display&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SMX is seeking a Senior Enterprise Solution Architect and Growth Lead for our State &amp;amp; Local Government practice. You will own product development, solution design, and technical delivery for complex, multi-agency cloud migration, application modernization, AI/ML, and data &amp;amp; analytics engagements.&amp;nbsp;This is a client-facing role with delivery accountability, team leadership, and business development responsibility. You will work directly with state executives, lead engineering teams, and contribute to proposals and capture efforts.&amp;nbsp;This is an application-layer role. Our clients are typically several years into a cloud journey - the infrastructure exists and is managed. What they need is someone who can look at a portfolio of aging agency applications and produce a credible, sequenced modernization path that survives contact with procurement, budget cycles, and a risk-averse security review.Our SLG application portfolio is predominantly Microsoft-stack at mixed levels of modernity, including C#, ASP.NET Core, legacy .NET Framework 4.8, SQL Server 2019+, React.js/JavaScript, Angular/TypeScript, and AWS cloud services including Bedrock and SageMaker for AI/ML work.&amp;nbsp;This position is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;hybrid&lt;/strong&gt; supporting a Boston, MA based customer.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;ng-binding&quot;&gt;Essential Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and shape new business opportunities by proactively engaging state and local government stakeholders, mapping agency pain points to SMX capabilities, and building a qualified pipeline aligned to the practice&#39;s growth targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive strategic product and service development by translating market trends, client feedback, and competitive intelligence into new solution offerings, repeatable accelerators, and go-to-market strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to RFP/RFQ responses - write technical approaches, build solution architectures, and develop sales materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive new and existing partner relationships, and navigate multi-agency, multi-vendor environments with competing constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead solution architecture from discovery through implementation - producing architecture documents, decision records, and technical governance that meet FedRAMP Moderate, GovRAMP, HIPAA, CJIS, and IRS Pub 1075 requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead modernization assessments across agency application portfolios, delivering disposition recommendations (rehost / replatform / refactor / replace / retire) with effort, cost, and risk attached to each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical narrative through delivery - reference patterns and guardrails that keep implementation teams consistent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up and improve the operational side of modernized applications: deployment automation, observability, incident response patterns, and the SLOs that matter to the mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as trusted technical advisor to senior government executives; translate technical decisions into business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and grow delivery teams - set technical direction, run design and code reviews, own staffing plans and skills-gap decisions, and participate in hiring and performance conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor mid-level architects and engineers, and raise the technical bar across the practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-binding&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;ng-binding&quot;&gt;Required Skills/Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 15 years in enterprise technology - architecture, engineering, or technical consulting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years contributing to or leading business development and capture activities - pipeline development, client relationship management, win-theme development, and strategic pricing/teaming decisions in government professional services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years directly leading engineering teams, including technical direction, mentoring, hiring, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to identify market opportunities and shape solution offerings - translating emerging technology trends (AI/ML, data modernization, cloud) into productized service lines or reusable frameworks that drive revenue growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Application modernization depth - legacy to cloud-native (containerization, microservices, API-first), with ownership of at least two substantial modernization efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Application architecture, decomposition, and refactoring strategy across large agency portfolios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;API design, API management, and integration architecture across agency systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD pipeline design and release engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise across the .NET ecosystem: C#, ASP.NET Core, and .NET Framework 4.8 - with demonstrated experience moving Framework applications forward incrementally rather than betting on a full rewrite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL Server (2019 or later) and Entity Framework / EF Core experience, including query performance tuning and zero-downtime migration strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working depth in at least one modern front-end framework - React.js/JavaScript or Angular/TypeScript - and enough command of both to set standards and review code across a mixed portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on AWS depth at the application layer: ECS/EKS, Lambda, API Gateway, Step Functions, RDS/Aurora, DynamoDB, SQS/SNS/EventBridge, IAM, CloudWatch, and infrastructure-as-code (Terraform or CDK).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI/ML practical experience (Bedrock, SageMaker, or equivalent; generative AI, RAG architectures).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data &amp;amp; analytics fluency - data lakes, analytics platforms, BI tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in regulated environments (FedRAMP Moderate, HIPAA, CJIS, IRS Pub 1075).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication - architecture documentation, executive presentations, and proposal writing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;ng-binding&quot;&gt;Desired Skills/Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS Solutions Architect - Professional, or equivalent certification with other cloud service providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;State and local government experience - procurement cycles, compliance, public-sector IT realities, state agencies such as Health and Human Services, Revenue, Transportation, or Labor and Workforce Development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medicaid or public benefits program technology experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oracle database environments and migration strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of Appian, ServiceNow, or low-code/BPM platforms in government sufficient to drive solutions that incorporate them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of enterprise data platforms and BI tooling (e.g., Snowflake, Informatica, Tableau) sufficient to drive solutions that incorporate them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
