&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support all aspects of Integrated Product Support (IPS) and product support requirements including research, analysis, development, integration, and coordination of logistics data to and from stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and review of acquisition-related documentation, including but not limited to Statements of Work (SOW}, Contract Data Requirements List (CDRL}, Data Item Description (DID), work breakdown structures, Integrated Master Schedules, and lifecycle cost estimates, as it relates to the acquisition of IPS requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support milestone activities including review of documentation and participation in design reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and assess FLRAA Supply Chain Risk Management (SCRM) in identifying and mitigating the risks related to sourcing, procurement, and conversion, as well as the coordination of technical management functions related to cyber security, quality manufacturing, diminishing manufacturing sources and material shortages (DMSMS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the analysis and assessment of logistics information required across product support integrators and product support providers, as necessary, to optimize the implementation of FLRAA product support strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in related Integrated Product Teams to include areas focused on Supply Chain Risk Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and assess FLRAA logistics operations in all areas of deployment across the FLRAA fleet to identify supply support deficiencies and recommend courses of action (COA) for deficiency resolution Analyze and assess product support arrangements to support the Government in validating arrangements as consistent with FLRAA product support strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development, implementation, and maintenance of current required logistics-related statutory and regulatory required program documentation, including but not limited to LCSP, Core Logistics Determination Estimate, Core Logistics and Sustainment Workloads Estimate, Independent Logistics Assessment, Item Unique Identification (IUID) Plan, Preservation and Storage of Unique Tooling Plan, and Replaced System Sustainment Plan.&lt;/li&gt;
